### **III. PROPOSED WORK** 

In this paper, we solve the previously mentioned problem by introducing a blockchain network at ground level with respect to the lands monitored. Each land will have an associated device as part of the block network that will carry out the verification process, thereby distributing the control and workload over two tiers. The devices will interact using the concept of fog computing over the decentralized blockchain network, forming a peer-to-peer network. The proposed solution results are compared with an existing solution in terms of cost, time complexity of computation, and overall computation cost. Fig. 2 represents the architectural diagram. 

