hierarchy has a bounding box that corresponds to its location on the constructed two-dimensional plane. The functions in the ingestion process then arrange the paragraphs in reading order, and the blocks are arranged in a pre-determined order for efficient processing in the later stages. Natural Language Processing (NLP) methods are applied to the stored data line by line to clean the data. The text data is first tokenized into words, and the stop words are removed from the data. This whole action takes place on a copy of the stored data. The reason the action is done on a copy is that the module will use the originally extracted data to compare the context generated in the later stages to improve efficiency. 

After the stop words are removed, a probabilistic language model is applied to the filtered data. This is a popular word and sequence analysis model that basically calculates the probability of a sentence containing a sequence of words. The calculated probabilities are used to determine the important entries in the document. A small amount of vector semantic and sequence labeling is applied wherever the probability calculation is not able to take place or the value is null or undefined. 

The next step involves candidate generation, which is basically the labeling of all the processed data to give a field to all attributes that are considered relevant and meaningful. This process uses various models that were trained on web data for sequence and expression matching of the given text. These models are also capable of performing regular expression matching and heuristic labeling to get the best results. To support all field types in the given system, we assign various candidate generators, which notably use the entity extraction service available in the cloud to identify portions of the OCR text that correspond to a respective type. For example, all the dates (eg: due_date, assign_date, purchase_date) in a land document are considered candidates as per the information in the schema of the target value. Now the system ensures high recall by providing the candidate generators with mechanisms to have high recall and not focus on the precision aspect. The precision is mainly handled by the scoring and assignment processes. 

We use a two-step procedure to extract the proper data for each field extracted in accordance with the schema in the target value after the aforementioned process generates a collection of candidates. 

Firstly, we independently score each candidate using a neural model, assigning a score of [0, 1] to each candidate. Once the score is assigned, we then assign various scores to all the candidates in respective fields with extracted values considered to have a high probability of being a pair in that field. Providing a separation between the scoring process and the assignment process makes the system more efficient, provides representational learning, and allows complex business rules to be encoded while performing the assignment action wherever necessary. For instance, the date of purchase cannot proceed to the date of renewal 

in any given document, so these kinds of modifications and checks can be performed automatically and with ease. 



