The next step is using the unique concept of attend, copy, and parse, which uses the above-mentioned processes in sync to give us the desired output. The attend method basically parses through all the information generated by the ingestion process and applies candidate generation and CNN to the necessary information based on the scores provided by the scorer method. For each iteration, the context method provides the context or relevance of the information as per the requirement based on its learning through web-based models. For example, the date fields are iterated over by the attend method, but they are only sent further for action when the context method provides a context for them based on deep learning techniques. A middleware method called copy stores information in the same way that data is stored in cache memory. The stored data in the copy method is just a failsafe method if an error arises and we need to roll back to the last data point of iteration through context. The final method parses and converts the data in a systematic format based on the context given by the context method and compares the said data with the model output from the assignment process. 

### 2) MODULE-1.2: LiLT TRANSFORMER MODEL EXTRACTOR 

Language-independent Layout Transformer (LiLT) is a framework that uses the concept of transformers to understand the semantics of structured documents. This transformer does not waste time on providing language support for context generation and is solely focused on the context generation of single-language documents. The transformer can be pre-trained on various single-language documents that are structured. The transformer can also be fine-tuned for other languages using existing pre-trained multilingual text-based models. LiLT uses a Bi-directional Attention Complementation Mechanism (BiACM) and widely recognized Masked Visual Language Modelling (MVLM) to execute the pre-training process. 

The major acting points of this module are: 

- Text Embedding similar to Module 1.1 

- Layout Embedding 

- Application of BiACM and MVLM as part of the pretraining 

