Interplanetary File System (IPFS) is a network protocol that allows the transfer of files over a decentralized network based on the principle of peer-to-peer computing. IPFS breaks down a particular file into various chunks, which are then distributed over a network of computers or machines that are under the IPFS network. IPFS uses Filecoin as a token of exchange for each transaction. IPFS works on name-based routing, where all the files are accessed through name-based routes and are reconstructed as per demand, giving the user the data they want and thereby saving time and computing resources. Ethereum helps in accessing the IPFS network on its own using various gateways. In our case, we use the Pinate gateway, which is an easy-to-use IPFS access gateway that leverages the power of Ethereum to distribute files over the IPFS network. Pinata also provides a user-friendly dashboard that helps in navigating and managing the files stored over the network. 

